      "writtenOn": "2024-11-11T19:32:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So IIUC you\u0027d prefer the module to set the path property that points to the key filepath? If this is the case, should this avbpubkey module be defined in external/.../Android.bp ?\n\nYes. Or define it in the root directory just so it\u0027s easier to autogenerate and reference the key. I think the make code should remain the same, let\u0027s not try to remove the make code for this, because we\u0027ll want a different module per-product which would require relying on the autogenerated module in production.\n\n\u003e Why do we need an autogenerated copy of the module (copy of the one defined in external/... I assume?)? Is it to install the artifact (*.avbpubkey file) to both system_other and product partition?\n\nYou don\u0027t need an autogenerated copy if there\u0027s already a module checked in, but 1) there only appears to be filegroups there, not something with installation rules and 2) `BOARD_AVB_SYSTEM_OTHER_KEY_PATH` could point you at a different key, in which case you\u0027d need a module that uses that key.",
      "parentUuid": "fdfc9f82_a1ab6c10",
      "revId": "e4629b25e2945445edccbd757232398015ad09f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
